        "name": "Shijou Saikyou League Serie A: Ace Striker",
        "summary": "Shijou Saikyou League Serie A: Ace Striker (\"Strongest League History Serie A: Ace Striker\") is a soccer game that features all eighteen clubs and its players from the 1994-95 Italian Serie A season. It is licensed by both the Italian Football League and the Associazione Italiana Calciatori (Italian Footballer's Association). One or two players can compete in friendly matches, a league contest or a penalty shoot-out mode.\n\nThe game has a horizontal perspective of the pitch and uses static cartoon cutaways whenever a goal is scored, which show the ball get past the goalkeeper or the striker celebrating. There are a number of different celebration animations that might play after each goal.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co4cvc.jpg",
